{"Title":"An Act relative to waiving education requirements for skilled veterans to be LPNs","BillNumber":"H3519","DocketNumber":"HD2278","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"KLG1","Name":"Kate Lipper-Garabedian","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KLG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:04:03.437"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"KLG1","Name":"Kate Lipper-Garabedian","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KLG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:04:03.4366667"},{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-03T16:06:33.9633333"},{"Id":"S_G2","Name":"Steven Ultrino","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_G2","ResponseDate":"2023-02-03T16:06:33.9633333"},{"Id":"BWM1","Name":"Brian W. Murray","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BWM1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-03T16:06:33.9633333"},{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-22T14:22:18.3566667"},{"Id":"PLC1","Name":"Peter Capano","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PLC1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-22T11:00:27.6733333"},{"Id":"RME1","Name":"Rodney M. Elliott","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RME1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-14T10:11:33.2833333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3519/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Lipper-Garabedian of Melrose, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3519) of Kate Lipper-Garabedian and others that the Board of Registration in Nursing be authorized to establish a waiver program for military personnel who satisfactorily complete medical training offered through the military.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 112 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting, after section 76B, the following section:-\r\n\tSection 76C. The board of registration in nursing shall create a waiver program for military personnel who satisfactorily complete medical training offered through the military so that they may sit for the licensed practical nursing certification without the need to graduate from an approved practical nursing program.\r\n\tSECTION 2. The department of public health shall promulgate regulations no later than January 1, 2024.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}